    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1957-p11.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The minute hand is \\(90^\\circ\\) clockwise from twelve. The hour hand is \\[ 2(30^\\circ)+\\frac14(30^\\circ)=67.5^\\circ \\] from twelve. Their smaller angle is \\(90^\\circ-67.5^\\circ=22.5^\\circ,\\) which is not listed.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "At \\(2:15,\\) the minute hand is at \\(90^\\circ\\) from twelve",
        "The hour hand has advanced one quarter of the \\(30^\\circ\\) interval from two to three"
      ],
